{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.brings_riemann_hurwitz","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.brings_riemann_hurwitz","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.brings_riemann_hurwitz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.brings_riemann_hurwitz","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_riemann_hurwitz.lean#L69-L82","doc":"**Lemma** ([`lem:brings-riemann-hurwitz`]):\nthe covering has degree `4`, total ramification `R_tot = 14`\n(derived from Riemann–Hurwitz with `g_Σ = 4`, `g_{ℙ¹} = 0`,\n`deg = 4`), distributed over `6` branch points.\n\nThe degree and branch-point count are geometric inputs; the\nramification `14` is **derived** by `norm_num`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:brings-riemann-hurwitz","label":"lem:brings-riemann-hurwitz","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-riemann-hurwitz.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext.R_tot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext.R_tot","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_riemann_hurwitz.lean#L62-L65","doc":"Total ramification, **defined** by the Riemann–Hurwitz formula\n`R_tot = (2 g_Σ − 2) − deg·(2 g_{ℙ¹} − 2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext.branch_is_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext.branch_is_six","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_riemann_hurwitz.lean#L56-L56","doc":"The `S₅`-symmetric branch-point count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext.n_branch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext.n_branch","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_riemann_hurwitz.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Number of branch points (`S₅`-symmetric ramification). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext.deg_is_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext.deg_is_four","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_riemann_hurwitz.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The covering degree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext.deg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext.deg","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_riemann_hurwitz.lean#L50-L50","doc":"Degree of the covering `π : Σ₄ → ℙ(V)` — geometric input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext.genus_P1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext.genus_P1","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_riemann_hurwitz.lean#L48-L48","doc":"The genus of the projective line. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext.g_P1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext.g_P1","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_riemann_hurwitz.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Genus of the target `ℙ¹` — geometric input `g(ℙ¹) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext.genus_Sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext.genus_Sigma","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_riemann_hurwitz.lean#L44-L44","doc":"The classical genus fact for Bring's surface. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext.g_Sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext.g_Sigma","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_riemann_hurwitz.lean#L42-L42","doc":"Genus of Bring's surface `Σ₄` — geometric input `g(Σ₄) = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_riemann_hurwitz.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsRiemannHurwitzContext","kind":"class","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_riemann_hurwitz.lean#L34-L56","doc":"Geometric context for the Riemann–Hurwitz lemma.\n\nThe data are the genuine geometric inputs (the two genera, the\ncovering degree, and the `S₅`-symmetric branch-point count).  The\ntotal ramification is *defined* from them via Riemann–Hurwitz (see\n`R_tot` below), so its value is derived rather than assumed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}